CAT = "cpaiscIncident"; SEG = "INC"
Q = [
("A failed login attempt is logged and blocked, with no harm to any system or data. It is best classified as a:",
 "Security event", ["Security incident", "Data breach", "Disaster"],
 "NIST defines an event as any observable occurrence. An incident actually or imminently jeopardizes the confidentiality, integrity or availability of information or systems."),
("Malware encrypts a file server and the business cannot reach its files. This is a:",
 "Security incident", ["Routine event only", "Planned change", "False positive"],
 "An occurrence that actually jeopardizes the availability of systems or data is an incident and triggers the response plan. Not every event becomes an incident, but this one has."),
("Cyber insurance mitigates the risk of a data breach mainly by:",
 "Transferring financial loss", ["Preventing attacks", "Detecting network intrusions earlier", "Avoiding the activity"],
 "Insurance is a risk transfer strategy: it pays for certain costs, such as forensics, notification and liability, but does nothing to stop or detect an attack."),
("Who decides, and how quickly, to notify regulators and customers during an active cyber incident is best set out in the:",
 "Incident response plan", ["Business impact analysis", "Acceptable use policy", "Change management policy"],
 "An incident response plan names roles, responsibilities, steps and timelines, including communications. A business impact analysis ranks processes for recovery but does not run the response."),
("After confirming malware on an employee's laptop, which step usually comes first?",
 "Isolate it from the network", ["Reimage the laptop straight away", "Notify every customer", "Restore it from backup"],
 "Containment comes before eradication and recovery, so the malware cannot spread. Reimaging first can also destroy evidence."),
("To test whether an entity responded to cybersecurity incidents in line with its incident response plan, an auditor should:",
 "Compare incident records to the plan", ["Read the plan's table of contents", "Ask IT staff if it was followed", "Review the cyber insurance policy terms"],
 "Inspecting incident records and comparing actions and timing with the plan gives evidence of operation. Inquiry alone is not enough."),
("Under the Trust Services Criteria, responding to identified security incidents by executing a defined incident response program is:",
 "CC7.4", ["CC7.2", "CC6.1", "CC8.1"],
 "CC7.4 covers responding to identified security incidents through a defined program. CC7.2 is monitoring system components for anomalies."),
("Under the Trust Services Criteria, judging whether security events could have caused a failure to meet objectives falls under:",
 "CC7.3", ["CC7.4", "CC7.5", "CC4.1"],
 "CC7.3 is evaluating security events to determine whether they are incidents. CC7.5 is recovering from identified incidents."),
("To understand how an entity builds security awareness among staff, an auditor would most likely begin by:",
 "Reviewing its training program", ["Running a penetration test", "Checking firewall rule sets", "Reading the disaster recovery plan"],
 "An awareness program is evidenced by its materials, attendance records and messages to personnel. A penetration test checks technical defenses."),
("Each finding in a security assessment report should give the issue, its cause, its effect and a:",
 "Recommendation", ["Legal opinion", "Penalty estimate", "Insurance claim"],
 "A useful finding tells management what to do about the issue. Legal opinions and penalties are outside the scope of a controls assessment."),
("A company sends staff fake phishing emails and tracks who clicks the link. This mainly tests:",
 "Security awareness", ["Firewall configuration", "Patch levels", "Backup recovery"],
 "Phishing simulations measure how well employees spot social engineering, which is the aim of awareness training. They say nothing about patches or backups."),
("In a SOC 2 examination, 3 of 25 sampled terminated users kept system access for 30 days after leaving. Which criterion area does the deviation relate to?",
 "CC6.2, removing credentials", ["CC8.1, authorizing changes", "CC3.2, identifying risks", "A1.1, capacity planning"],
 "CC6.2 covers registering, authorizing and removing user credentials when access is no longer authorized. Late removal is a deviation in that logical access control."),
]
